I have a possible solution to the problem that all of us in the Think C
community have had compiling Nethack 3.1.x, which is setup as an MPW
project.  Although Think's C 5.0 and 6.0 are full featured solutions that
can compile most of the project, and the source has hooks for Think C, the
biggest problem stems around Think C's inability to act like a UNIX
environment, and therefore be able to handle MPW Tools and Unix-type
Makefiles.

After pouring through the manual for Think C 6.0, I found out that the
product supports the MPW Toolserver, which is a stripped down version of
MPW.  In theory, you could feed this thing a makefile and build the
application this way instead of having Think C doing its version of a
"make".  The problem is that the Toolserver costs money from APDA, and
isn't a product that most of us have, or is probably willing to get just to
build this app, since someone will probably build one from MPW and post in
the next few months ;-).

